  "id": "ca_hue",
  "name": "Ca Huế (Huế chamber song)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Chamber song of Huế that grew among the aristocratic and literati circles of the Nguyễn capital and is still performed by Huế singers and instrumentalists, including on boats on the Perfume River. Its repertoire divides into điệu Bắc pieces of bright character and điệu Nam pieces of sorrowful character such as Nam ai and Nam bình, sung by a solo singer with đàn tranh zither, đàn tỳ bà, đàn nguyệt, đàn bầu and bamboo flute.",
  "recipe": "classic modern ca huế, art Music, southeast Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. dan tranh, dan ty ba, dan nguyet, dan bau, sao truc. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
